Zoong Pham <dpham@mercy_dot_com.au> writes:
>How big are the files/directories that you tried to transfer?
>Have you tried with different flags?
>-avrz works for me on the same version of Tru64.
>I use rsync-2.5.4

If you have a lot of files and directories either side of the rsync can
consume all the available swap space.  Check on the Tru-64 lazy-swap
settings on both sides to make sure that maximum swap space is available.

You can break the rsync up into smaller pieces - this is also wise if you
have an unstable network.

Another potential problem is a bad spot on the disk - look for disk errors.

Later

Mark Hittinger
