Roman Schicht wrote:
> Hi,
>
> today i installed a second NIC in my 1000A.
>
>
> After the reboot there was no tu1 (tu0 is the primary NIC and is
> still working).

if the card uses the same tulip chipset as the tu0 card then it should
just work. If not you can allways rebuild the kernel.
From the >>> prompt,
boot -file genvmunix
login as root
doconfig
This will build a new kernel
Copy the old one(/vmunix) somewhere safe, then copy this one into place and
reboot using the new kernel.
This should show an extra card.

If this doesn't work, please include in your next post the output from
show config at the console prompt and the output of ifconfig -a at the
root prompt when booted from genvmunix.

Adam




