If you want a REAL Cluster try VMS.

In 1983 the word cluster was originally used to describe a group of
VMS systems because astronomers refer to a group stars as a Cluster.
The code name for the VAX780 was STAR.

BTW A Galaxy is cluster of Clusters.  VMS has Galaxy support (Cluster of
clusters)
on Wildfire hardware.

A VMS cluster can be homogenous or heterogeneous but it is real.

Unix even Tru64 can only pretend to provide what was available 20 years ago.

G

